{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Josh Groban feels like a natural next choice after Stages because I want more rich, melodic singing; Partners also appeals through its vocal duets and musical-theater feel.",
    "Passione fits the romantic classical-crossover singing I enjoy in Amor & Pasion and A Musical Affair, while Melody Road connects with my earlier interest in Neil Diamond's The Bang Years."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Man Against Machine connects with my past country listening, but that connection matters less today than my desire for gentle, vocal-focused music.",
    "Christmas reflects a past seasonal interest rather than what I want now, and The Best ...So Far gives me too little information to judge a musical connection."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Having listened to country albums seems to have been taken as a reason to offer more country regardless of the mood I currently want.",
    "My Christmas listening seems to have been treated as an ongoing preference rather than something I may want only at particular times."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest relaxing classical selection, alongside my vocal albums, makes gentle orchestral textures and expressive singing especially appealing right now.",
    "Broadly appealing vocals are not enough to make every album equally compelling: I would choose the orchestral and classical-crossover appeal of Josh Groban or Passione before 25 or To Be Loved today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in expressive singers, but give some older country and seasonal interests more weight than my current preference for gentle, orchestral vocal music."
}"}
